#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""run-preflight: read-only checks before a hardware run (TP-024). Host only; never touches the phone, no adb/fastboot.

  tools/run-preflight [--json] [--root-sha SHA] [--margin S] [--writer --changed-vs "LABEL: ONE VARIABLE"] -- tools/xrun|tools/probe-run ARGS...
  tools/run-preflight --gen-bootargs [--check [--patches-only]] [--pristine DIR]   regenerate tools/bootargs-known.txt (--check: exit 1 if stale;
                                        --patches-only: no pristine tree, recheck only the xnu/patches rows; caller tools/validate-repo.py, gate)
  tools/run-preflight --userdata-check   (tools/xrun, before the build; first prints `FLASH: last=UTC reason=TEXT today=N` or `FLASH: none recorded`, R54) exit 2 unless the newest flashed-userdata.txt line is an iOS root flash
                                        (64-hex sha256; `erased ...` from tools/fboot-android or no file = ERROR); bypass XRUN_USERDATA_BYPASS="reason >= 10 chars"
  tools/run-preflight --gate-check ram|flash   (T-f32e) only the gate rule: exit 0 and `RESULT: PASS gate admitted-by=quick|formal|waiver` / exit 1 `RESULT: FAIL gate: why`.
                                        ram = tools/xrun, tools/probe-run (fastboot boot); flash = tools/fflash-userdata.sh (a quick gate is refused)
  tools/run-preflight --self-test

Checks (each names the antipattern that motivates it; SKIP = not enough verified information, never a silent pass):
  bootargs  xrun --args: every boot-arg NAME is parsed somewhere (tools/bootargs-known.txt, generated from pristine xnu-8796 +
            xnu/patches; tools/bootargs-extra.txt = hand-added names, each with a citation). A grep is a start, not proof.
  syntax    xrun --args: sweettouchpoke= must end with ';' (AP-10, patch 0093)
  reach     every --expect row is < every accepted stop row (a pattern with "stopped=" and row=N|M) (AP-27)
  timeout   probe-run --timeout (or the tools/probe-run default) >= max earlier wall of runs with the same build-arg option names
            (tools/runs stats --args --all-worktrees; probe-run writes run.args since review B2) + --margin (default 60 s, a guess) (AP-14/AP-22)
  form      every --expect containing "LINK summary" has "restore=ok" and "stopped=none" or "stopped=... row=N" (CR-08, review W3A-4 F1: a bare
            "LINK summary reached=S23" also matches stopped=fault|timeout and restore=FAILED); --writer needs --changed-vs "<label>: <variable>" (CR-08)
  cmdline   xrun: the exact boot-args line of this run, from `tools/xrun --print-bootargs ARGS` (TP-040: xrun's own flag handling incl. the
            sweetremote=1 it adds itself (AP-154), then build-xnu-image.sh's XNU_IMAGE_ARGS_ONLY hook) must fit mkpayload's field (its BOOT_LINE_LENGTH,
            imported, incl. the NUL: 2048 with xnu patch 0320, 1024 with 0176 alone, 608 before; tools/mkpayload.py); the detail lists the implicit boot-args counted. Fails BEFORE the flash/build.
  adt       xrun without --adt: research/ipsw-x/d22ap.adt must resolve in this worktree, else mkadt silently drops /product (AP-144, TP-038 a)
  platform  xrun: that same boot-args line has unentitled_ios_sim_launch=1 (every token of that name, none other) AND the --kernel file's
            "@(#)VERSION:" string ends in a DEVELOPMENT_* objroot (pristine config/version.c:39, config/newvers.pl:19,73). Without both,
            xnu-8796 refuses every iOS binary spawned without a spawn-attr platform, launchd included (EACCES, WRONG_PLATFORM:
            pristine bsd/kern/kern_exec.c:7391-7413; the tunable exists only #if DEBUG || DEVELOPMENT, :195-197, :7395; research 97 5a.1).
            A missing --kernel file is SKIP (xrun itself refuses it, tools/xrun:48), never PASS.
  gate      shim/out/gate.result is "GATE PASS <HEAD short hash>" (AP-21; check-all.sh writes it) AND the work tree is clean (review B3). A `quick:` PASS (tools/gate --quick --changed)
            is enough for these RAM-boot tools ONLY together with shim/out/lint-first.result `LINT-FIRST PASS <HEAD>` (tools/gate-lint-first); the detail says admitted-by=quick|formal
            (T-f32e, user order 2026-11-02, RULES R28); a flash or a trunk merge still needs the formal gate; PREFLIGHT_GATE_WAIVER="reason >= 10 chars" (USER-approved runs only, per command) skips this check only, printed as GATE WAIVED and marked gate_waiver in the xrun summary
  root      newest line of flashed-userdata.txt is an iOS root flash whose sha256 == --root-sha (an `erased` line FAILs; SKIP without --root-sha)
  lock      phone lock free or held by the caller (tools/phone-lock status/check)
  recovery  xrun: a USB-free self-reset is armed (--restart S>0 or --args sweetrestart=S) or the run plan has a line `no-recovery: <why, >= 10 chars>` (T-322d;
            also refused by tools/xrun through --intent-check, exit 2). Covers an XNU-stage hang only: sweetrestart is armed in XNU (xnu patch 0083), the shim arms no
            reset and disables the bootloader watchdogs (shim/shim.c disable_bluejay_watchdog); a shim-stage hang needs the PR-4 petted watchdog (T-5d2f).
Known gaps (LOW): xrun wall time is not compared; probe runs from before run.args existed have no history; the three userland boot-args (wdt_test,
ignition_level, launchd_unsecure_cache) FAIL until a cited bootargs-extra.txt entry exists (spec-conformant).
Not implemented (no verified source yet, listed as SKIP): image meta vs HEAD, --overlay after migration finished, the build's recorded root.
Last line: RESULT: PASS | FAIL <check>: <reason>   Exit 0 pass / 1 a check failed / 2 bad arguments or internal error.
Env (tests): PREFLIGHT_ROOT repo root, PREFLIGHT_KNOWN/PREFLIGHT_EXTRA name lists, ARTIFACTS, FLASH_STATE, FLASH_REASONS, RUNS_ROOT, PHONE_LOCK_DIR.
"""
